    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with a clear focus on exploiting favorable pitching matchups to stabilize our Roto standing. Our premier play is **Kyle Tucker** (79.68), whose matchup against Merrill Kelly (5.13 xERA) provides an elite ceiling. He is closely followed by **Andy Pages** (73.64), who also benefits from the soft matchup against Kelly and the high-leverage #2 spot in the order. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (72.22) rounds out our top tier, drawing a significant boost from a dynamic platoon advantage against Mahle (4.26 xERA), allowing him to leverage his 72.22 efficiency score to anchor the middle infield. While **Gunnar Henderson** (63.19) faces the toughest test of our starters against Nathan Eovaldi, his elite #1 batting position and high-speed profile make him an essential start despite the SP skill penalty.\n\nThe most difficult personnel decision centered on **Liam Hicks**, who narrowly missed the starting cut with a 39.67 score. While his platoon edge against Logan Gilbert was statistically significant, his efficiency floor fell just below our 40.0 threshold, and his poor park factors pushed him to the bench in favor of more consistent matchups. We are keeping a close watch on **Drake Baldwin**, who sits at 58.11; while he is currently in the lineup, his proximity to the marginal category means we are monitoring weather updates, as Max Fried represents a challenging southpaw opponent. We remain without the services of **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** and **Luis Robert Jr.** due to lineup/rest status, leaving our depth\u2014including players like **Jordan Westburg**, **Sam Antonacci**, **Josh Jung**, **Coby Mayo**, **Dominic Smith**, **Curtis Mead**, and **Luis Lara**\u2014ready to rotate in should late-scratch scenarios arise. **Nasim Nunez** earns a sneaky start at 63.69 thanks to his impressive 19% SP skill bonus, which helps offset the bottom-of-the-order risk against Petty.",
